==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*30 [[Cerberus Kids]] (300%) spawn, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16~20 seconds<sup>480f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 32~40 seconds<sup>960f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Cerberus Kids]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] (300%) spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
**5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**5 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Seal Level: 30 or higher.

Bring [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]]/[[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] as meatshields. You'll want at least three piercing attackers like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], and [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] to snipe the Condemned Pengs and Aku Gories; even at Lv.30, they pack a heavy punch and can wear down their numbers until victory is achieved. Just stall the opening peons until you're at a good enough wallet level, then prepare for a full-scale ambush. There's no money concerns here, as the countless peons will supply you with plenty.

As with other XP stages, this stage has a high base XP drop—around 800 thousand XP with [[Fruit Treasures]]—so you can bring [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] for significant bonus XP.

